# make lint: the scripts that run on the Echo (scripts/system, scripts/device), as POSIX sh.  What is left out is style
# these scripts use on purpose, not bugs:
# - paths and word lists are unquoted on purpose: the Echo's paths have no spaces, and lists of services, files and
#   iptables arguments are meant to split (SC2086, SC2046, SC2231)
# - device.conf and hassmic.conf are sourced from paths known only on the Echo (SC1090, SC1091)
# - `a && b || c` where c is meant to run when either fails (SC2015)
# - export of a command substitution whose status does not matter (SC2155)
# - read without -r of /proc values that hold no backslashes (SC2162)
# - ps | grep and ls in probe.sh: toybox, a debugging aid (SC2009, SC2012)
disable=SC2086,SC2046,SC2231,SC1090,SC1091,SC2015,SC2155,SC2162,SC2009,SC2012
